  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes typecheck. I haven't run it in a browser or run `vite build`.\n\nIt loads `/assets/soldier.glb` through `defineModelAssets`. The sha256 and clip list come from the recipe in docs/agents/recipes.md, so I did not compute the hash from the file. If the hash doesn't match, the model won't load.\n\n- **Scene:** the soldier is scaled to 1.8 units tall on a ground plane. A perspective camera frames the whole character. One directional light casts the shadow onto the ground, with a hemisphere light for fill.\n- **Animation:** it starts on `Idle`. Pressing `R` cross-fades to `Run` over 0.4 s, and pressing `I` cross-fades back to `Idle` over 0.4 s.\n- **Eval hooks:** `window.__EVAL__.clip()` returns the target clip name as soon as a fade starts. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true after the model loads and two animation frames have run.",
